<title>USA: U.S. 2-year note auction high yield 5.885 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. 2-year note auction high yield 5.885 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Treasury said its Dutch bidding auction of two-year notes produced these results:</p>
<p>			 2-YEAR NOTES DUE FEB 28, 1999</p>
<p>			     $17.507 BILLION AUCTION</p>
<p>	     YIELD			  PRICE	COUPON</p>
<p> HIGH	5.885    Awarded At	99.981	5.875</p>
<p> MEDIAN    5.865    High Yield	NOT GIVEN  Percent</p>
<p> LOW	 5.820    94 Percent	NOT GIVEN</p>
<p>	   Cover - (Bids Over Amount Sold)    =  2.21 Times</p>
<p> U.S. TREASURY (GOVERNMENT DEBT)		 MATURITY 28.Feb.99</p>
<p> MATURITY/TYPE    2-YEAR NOTES		   PAY DATE 28.Feb.97</p>
<p> TYPE OF DEBT     STRAIGHT			 LAUNCHED 25.Feb.97</p>
<p> ISSUED/ACCEPTED  17.507 BLN USD		 CUSIP    9128272K7</p>
<p> BIDS SUBMITTED   38.699			   COUNTRY	  USA</p>
<p> NONCOMPETITIVE    1.321				DUTCH AUCTION</p>
<p> NY FED DISTRICT    N.A.			   COUPON	 5.875</p>
<p> FOREIGN INSTITN   1.750			   PRICE	 99.981</p>
<p> BIDDING RANGE    5.820-5.885 PCT		YIELD-HIGH   5.885</p>
<p>KEY (HIGH) YIELD DOWN FROM 5.984 PCT AT AUCTION ON 22.JAN.97 KEY (HIGH) YIELD LOWEST SINCE 5.874 PCT AT AUCTION 18.DEC.96</p>
